  "notes": "はっと describes the psychological moment of sudden awareness or being startled.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- はっと{気|き}がつく: to suddenly realize\n- はっとする: to be startled, to be struck\n- はっと{目|め}が{覚|さ}める: to wake up with a start\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ぱっと: suddenly (more physical/visual)\n- ふと: suddenly, casually (gentler realization)",
